{"text": "Interestingly if you are sad. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Then listening to sad music. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Can sometimes improve your mood. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> You might suppose. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That the last thing that would help. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If you are having a bad day. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Is to play something that reflects that negativity. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Why would not a sad person listen to happy music. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The reason is that when you are feeling down or depressed. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It is often because you feel misunderstood. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That the people around you do not appreciate what you are going through. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If you were to listen to happy music. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> While in this state. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It would only amplify. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That feeling of detachment. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> On the other hand if you put on the right piece of sad music. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> You can say to yourself. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That is exactly how I feel. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> This musician understands me. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> So the sad music turns out to be soothing. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> A companion to your misery. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> As it were.", "alignment": {"characters": ["I", "n", "t", "e", "r", "e", "s", "t", "i", "n", "g", "l", "y", " ", "i", "f", " ", "y", "o", "u", " ", "a", "r", "e", " ", "s", "a", "d", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "T", "h", "e", "n", " ", "l", "i", "s", "t", "e", "n", "i", "n", "g", " ", "t", "o", " ", "s", "a", "d", " ", "m", "u", "s", "i", "c", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "C", "a", "n", " ", "s", "o", "m", "e", "t", "i", "m", "e", "s", " ", "i", "m", "p", "r", "o", "v", "e", " ", "y", "o", "u", "r", " ", "m", "o"